    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41086" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστροφ-άδην</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turning this way and that
			way</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτεῖνε δ᾽</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">επιστροφάδην</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.483
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύπτε δ᾽ ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				21.20
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.308
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.184
			</span></i> (or perh., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστρεφῶς</span>
			, <i>earnestly, vehemently</i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. βαδίζειν</span> wander
				<i>back- and forwards,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				210
			</span></i>; <i>on all sides</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.79
			</span></i>: Poet. and late Prose, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. κτείνειν,
				ἀναιρεῖν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.33
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				320
			</span></i>.</div>
